#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087475 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/id #uuid "73491cdd-3c8c-5203-b403-6176f6eb2917" :question/math-academy-id "e-5280" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z$, shown in the following Argand diagram, in exponential form.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/898/Source/Images/a0fe46e109e3784d66675d033d5fdbd8.png)" :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= x + \\textrm{i}y \\\\\n&=-3 + 2\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form\n\n$$\nz = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nr= \\mid z \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arg(z)\n$$\n\nwe first calculate $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr = \\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-3)^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\arg (z) &= π - \\mid \\arctan (\\frac{y}{x}) \\mid \\\\\n&= π - \\mid \\arctan (\\frac{2}{3}) \\mid \\\\\n&= π - 0.588 \\\\\n&= 2.554\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places.\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{13}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=2.554\n$$\n\ninto\n\n$$\nz=re^{\\textrm{i} \\theta}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\nz = \\sqrt{13}\\,\\textrm{e}^{2.554\\,\\textrm{i}}\\,\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087476 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/id #uuid "339f9406-2f1a-52de-959b-23a7fe73ef68" :question/math-academy-id "e-5282" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=4+4\\textrm{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form\n\n$$\nz = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nr= \\mid z \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arg(z)\n$$\n\nwe first calculate $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr = \\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nθ = \\arg (z) &= \\arctan (\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\\n&= \\arctan (1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{π}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nr=4\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\ninto\n\n$$\nz=re^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\nz = 4\\sqrt{2}\\,\\textrm{e}^{\\pi\\textrm{i}/4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c49e3d4-1141-5e86-9dc0-07a769f8d693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266098} {:answer/id #uuid "6b55a12f-e52a-5d98-84d6-20878083f7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.338\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266099} {:answer/id #uuid "32aa2e4b-9f77-5cb7-8958-e69543136db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.989\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266100} {:answer/id #uuid "4c394217-aa5e-5f73-8b5a-b6cc3654b8ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266101} {:answer/id #uuid "f92c6ec2-5174-5770-b4fe-0716b26824e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.338\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c49e3d4-1141-5e86-9dc0-07a769f8d693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266098} :answer-field/id #uuid "e293d670-8dd1-5590-974c-860db0453b5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de095b2a-fbb0-51f2-b405-5336c443d2b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-8076" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=5-\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-1}{5})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{5})| \\\\  & ≈2\\pi -0.197\\,39… \\\\  & ≈6.086.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{26}$ and $\\theta =6.086$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}]}
